/-!
# Normalization and base change to the completion

Let `(A, m)` be a Noetherian local ring, let `X` be a scheme locally of finite type over
`Spec A`, and let `Y = X ×_{Spec A} Spec A^` be the base change of `X` to the `m`-adic completion
`A^` of `A`.  If the complement of the special fibre in `Y` is normal, then the normalization
`X^ν → X` is a finite morphism, and the base change of `X^ν` to `Spec A^` is the normalization
of `Y`.

Both assertions are Zariski local on `X`, so the question reduces to an affine `X = Spec B` of
finite type over `A`, where `Y = Spec (B ⊗[A] A^)`.  The completion is faithfully flat over `A`
and induces an isomorphism `A ⧸ m ≅ A^ ⧸ m A^`, hence an isomorphism between the quotients of `B`
and of `B ⊗[A] A^` by the ideal generated by a finite generating family `a` of `m`.  The
normalization of `Y` is finite because `A^` is a Nagata ring, and over the basic open of each
`a i` it is an isomorphism: that locus lies in the complement of the special fibre, where `Y` is
normal by hypothesis.  Formal glueing along the ideal generated by `a` therefore descends the
coordinate ring of the normalization of `Y` to a finite normal `B`-algebra `D`.  Over every
generic point of `Spec B` the morphism `Spec D → Spec B` is an isomorphism — over the basic opens
of the `a i` by construction, and over the primes containing `a` because there the fibre of
`Y → Spec B` is the spectrum of the residue field — so the residue fields at the generic points
of `Spec B` lift to `Spec D` with dense image.  The universal property of the normalization then
identifies `Spec D` with the normalization of `Spec B` and its base change with the normalization
of `Y`.

## Main results

Both results live in the namespace `AlgebraicGeometry.SemistableReduction`.

* `isFinite_normalization_of_isNormal_complementSpecialFiber_completion`:
  the normalization of `X` is a finite morphism.
* `exists_iso_pullback_normalization_completion_of_isNormal_complementSpecialFiber`:
  the base change of the normalization of `X` to `Spec A^` is the normalization of `Y`,
  compatibly with the normalization morphism of `Y`.

Together they are the two assertions of Tag 0BG9.

## Implementation notes

The complement of the special fibre is `complementSpecialFiber`, the inverse image of the
punctured spectrum of the completion; it is the same open subscheme whose normality is supplied by
`isNormal_complementSpecialFiber_baseChange_adicCompletion`.  Every
scheme occurring here is locally Noetherian, so the hypothesis on irreducible components of
quasi-compact opens that `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.normalization` requires is available
canonically; it is spelled out as a `let`-bound proof inside both statements, so that the two
normalization morphisms named in them are the same terms the reader would write.

The descent step is a formal glueing argument for modules and algebras along the ideal generated
by a finite generating family of the maximal ideal.  Its ingredients — the glueing datum obtained
by replacing the generic piece, the algebra of compatible sections, and the identification of its
localizations — are private to this module, being used only to produce the descended algebra.

Finiteness of the normalization is Zariski local on the target, which is `IsFinite` being local at
the target; the comparison over an affine chart uses the isomorphism `X^ν = X ×_Y Y^ν` for an
étale morphism, `AlgebraicGeometry.isPullback_normalizationSchemeMap_of_etale`, applied to the
inclusions of the members of an affine open cover.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BG9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BG9)
-/

